The **In-App Over-The-Air (OTA) APK Update System** has been designed and implemented.

---

### What Was Built on the Backend:

1. **Database Schema**:
   - Created [`migrations/003_add_app_releases.sql`](file:///Users/dhruv/Desktop/BAPA%27S/Attendy-backend/migrations/003_add_app_releases.sql) & updated [`migrations/schema.sql`](file:///Users/dhruv/Desktop/BAPA%27S/Attendy-backend/migrations/schema.sql) with the `app_releases` table.
   - Stores `version_code`, `version_name`, `apk_url`, `release_notes`, `is_force_update`, and active rollout status.

2. **REST Endpoints**:
   - `GET /api/hrm/app-updates/check?platform=android&version_code=<build_number>`: Checks if an active update exists.
   - `POST /api/hrm/app-updates/publish`: Owner endpoint to publish a new APK release and set rollout.
   - `GET /api/hrm/app-updates/releases`: Owner listing of all releases.
   - `PUT /api/hrm/app-updates/releases/:id/rollout`: Owner endpoint to switch or rollback active releases.
   - `DELETE /api/hrm/app-updates/releases/:id`: Owner endpoint to remove releases.

3. **CLI Helper**:
   - Created [`scripts/publish_release.js`](file:///Users/dhruv/Desktop/BAPA%27S/Attendy-backend/scripts/publish_release.js) to publish APK releases directly from terminal.

4. **API Documentation**:
   - Updated [`API_DOCS.md`](file:///Users/dhruv/Desktop/BAPA%27S/Attendy-backend/API_DOCS.md).

